<title>AUSTRALIA: Rugby union-New South Wales beat Queensland 33-9.</title>
<headline>Rugby union-New South Wales beat Queensland 33-9.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>New South Wales beat Queensland 33-9 (halftime 10-6) in a State of the Union rugby union match on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>New South Wales - Tries: Manuel Edmonds, Fili Finau, Scott Bowen, David Campese. Conversions: Manuel Edmonds, Scott Bowen. Penalties: Manuel Edmonds (3).</p>
<p>Queensland - Penalties: Tyron Mandrusiak (3).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
